---
title: Description
description: Renders supplementary help text for a field and associates it with the control via aria-describedby.
---

`Description` renders a `<div>` with hint text for the current field. The enclosing [Control](/docs/components/control) automatically adds the description's ID to the input's `aria-describedby`, so screen readers announce the hint when the control receives focus.

For the common case — one description per field — prefer the [owned `description` snippet on Field](/docs/components/field), which puts the association in server-rendered HTML. Use standalone `Description` when the layout needs the hint somewhere the owned slot can't reach, or when a control should have several descriptions.

## Minimal example

```svelte title="src/routes/settings/settings-form.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { untrack } from "svelte";
	import { superForm, type SuperValidated } from "sveltekit-superforms";
	import { Control, Description, Field, Label } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
	import type { SettingsData } from "./schema.js";

	let { validated }: { validated: SuperValidated<SettingsData> } = $props();

	const form = superForm(untrack(() => validated));
	const { form: formData } = form;
</script>

<Field {form} name="bio" fieldErrors>
	<Control>
		{#snippet children({ props })}
			<Label>Bio</Label>
			<textarea {...props} bind:value={$formData.bio}></textarea>
		{/snippet}
	</Control>
	<Description>Shown on your public profile. 250 characters max.</Description>
</Field>
```

## Replacing the rendered element

The `child` snippet swaps the `<div>` for your own element. Spread the supplied `props` — they carry the `id` and register the mounted element with the field, so a child that ignores them produces no association.

```svelte title="src/routes/settings/inline-description.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Control, Description, Label } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
	import { form, formData } from "./form.svelte.js";
</script>

<Control>
	{#snippet children({ props })}
		<Label>Username</Label>
		<input {...props} bind:value={$formData.username} />
	{/snippet}
</Control>
<Description>
	{#snippet child({ props })}
		<small {...props} class="hint">Letters, numbers and underscores only.</small>
	{/snippet}
</Description>
```

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| ---- | ---- | ------- | ----------- |
| `id` | `string` | generated | The description's ID. Generated with Svelte's `$props.id()` when omitted, stable between server rendering and hydration. |
| `ref` | `HTMLElement \| null` | `null` | Bindable reference to the rendered element. |
| `children` | `Snippet` | — | The description content. |
| `child` | `Snippet<[{ props }]`> | — | Replaces the `<div>`; spread the supplied `props` onto your own container. |
| `...rest` | `HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>` | — | Additional attributes (`class`, `style`, event handlers) merged onto the container. |

The merged attributes are `id`, `data-fs-description`, and `data-fs-error` while the field has errors.

## Behavior notes

- **Requires a field scope.** `Description` reads context from an enclosing [Field](/docs/components/field), [Fieldset](/docs/components/fieldset) or [ElementField](/docs/components/element-field); outside one it throws.
- **Association registers on mount.** The standalone component discovers its target when the element mounts and withdraws it on unmount. That means the association is absent from server-rendered HTML — if you need `aria-describedby` with JavaScript disabled, use the owned `description` snippet on the field scope instead.
- **Several descriptions coexist.** Multiple descriptions (standalone or owned) for one field are merged and deduplicated into a single space-separated `aria-describedby`, with the owned ID first.
- **Error styling.** `data-fs-error` lets you restyle the hint when validation fails.

## When to use the hooks instead

A custom control component can declare its own description container with the `descriptionId` getter on `useFormField`. Keep the element rendered while its ID is supplied; return `null` or `undefined` from the getter to withdraw it. See [Custom controls](/docs/recipes/custom-controls).

## See also

- [Field](/docs/components/field) — its owned `description` snippet is the SSR-safe alternative.
- [FieldErrors](/docs/components/field-errors) — the error counterpart, also associated through `aria-describedby`.
- [Accessibility](/docs/guides/accessibility) — how the association model works end to end.
